# 11. Database Schema

The simplified MVP uses **8 PostgreSQL tables**.

```text
1. departments
2. profiles
3. budgets
4. expense_policies
5. approval_rules
6. expenses
7. expense_approvals
8. audit_logs
```

Supabase Auth independently provides:

```text
auth.users
```

Do not create `auth.users` manually.

---

# 12. Database Relationships

```text
auth.users
     │
     ▼
profiles
     │
     ├──────────────┐
     ▼              ▼
departments      expenses
     │              │
     ▼              ├───────────────┐
budgets             ▼               ▼
              expense_approvals   audit_logs


expense_policies
        │
        ▼
     expenses


approval_rules
        │
        ▼
     expenses
```

---

# 13. Table 1 — departments

Purpose:

Stores organization departments.

Columns:

```text
id              UUID PK
name            TEXT
description     TEXT
created_at      TIMESTAMPTZ
```

SQL:

```sql
CREATE TABLE public.departments (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    name TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,
    description TEXT,
    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW()
);
```

---

# 14. Table 2 — profiles

Purpose:

Application-specific user information.

Supabase Auth handles authentication through `auth.users`.

Columns:

```text
id              UUID PK / FK auth.users
full_name       TEXT
employee_code   TEXT
role            TEXT
department_id   UUID FK
created_at      TIMESTAMPTZ
updated_at      TIMESTAMPTZ
```

Allowed roles:

```text
employee
manager
finance
admin
```

SQL:

```sql
CREATE TABLE public.profiles (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY REFERENCES auth.users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    full_name TEXT NOT NULL,
    employee_code TEXT UNIQUE,
    role TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'employee'
        CHECK (role IN ('employee', 'manager', 'finance', 'admin')),
    department_id UUID REFERENCES public.departments(id) ON DELETE SET NULL,
    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),
    updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW()
);
```

---

# 15. Table 3 — budgets

Purpose:

Stores department-level budgets defined by administrators.

Columns:

```text
id              UUID PK
department_id   UUID FK
fiscal_year     INTEGER
total_amount    NUMERIC
created_by      UUID FK
created_at      TIMESTAMPTZ
updated_at      TIMESTAMPTZ
```

Important:

Do NOT permanently store:

```text
spent_amount
remaining_amount
```

Calculate those values from actual expenses.

SQL:

```sql
CREATE TABLE public.budgets (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),

    department_id UUID NOT NULL
        REFERENCES public.departments(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,

    fiscal_year INTEGER NOT NULL,

    total_amount NUMERIC(14,2) NOT NULL
        CHECK (total_amount >= 0),

    created_by UUID
        REFERENCES public.profiles(id) ON DELETE SET NULL,

    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),
    updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),

    UNIQUE (department_id, fiscal_year)
);
```

---

# 16. Table 4 — expense_policies

Purpose:

Defines reimbursement and expense rules.

Columns:

```text
id
category
max_amount_per_transaction
max_amount_per_day
receipt_required
description
is_active
created_by
created_at
```

SQL:

```sql
CREATE TABLE public.expense_policies (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),

    category TEXT NOT NULL,

    max_amount_per_transaction NUMERIC(14,2)
        CHECK (max_amount_per_transaction >= 0),

    max_amount_per_day NUMERIC(14,2)
        CHECK (max_amount_per_day >= 0),

    receipt_required BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT TRUE,

    description TEXT,

    is_active BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT TRUE,

    created_by UUID
        REFERENCES public.profiles(id) ON DELETE SET NULL,

    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW()
);
```

---

# 17. Table 5 — approval_rules

Purpose:

Defines approval hierarchy.

Columns:

```text
id
min_amount
max_amount
required_role
approval_order
is_active
created_by
created_at
```

SQL:

```sql
CREATE TABLE public.approval_rules (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),

    min_amount NUMERIC(14,2) NOT NULL
        CHECK (min_amount >= 0),

    max_amount NUMERIC(14,2)
        CHECK (
            max_amount IS NULL
            OR max_amount >= min_amount
        ),

    required_role TEXT NOT NULL
        CHECK (
            required_role IN ('manager', 'finance', 'admin')
        ),

    approval_order INTEGER NOT NULL
        CHECK (approval_order > 0),

    is_active BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT TRUE,

    created_by UUID
        REFERENCES public.profiles(id) ON DELETE SET NULL,

    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW()
);
```

---

# 18. Table 6 — expenses

This is the central/main table.

Columns:

```text
id
employee_id
department_id
amount
currency
category
merchant
expense_date
description
invoice_number
receipt_path
status
policy_status
risk_level
ai_recommendation
ai_summary
ai_analysis
submitted_at
created_at
updated_at
```

SQL:

```sql
CREATE TABLE public.expenses (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),

    employee_id UUID NOT NULL
        REFERENCES public.profiles(id) ON DELETE RESTRICT,

    department_id UUID NOT NULL
        REFERENCES public.departments(id) ON DELETE RESTRICT,

    amount NUMERIC(14,2) NOT NULL
        CHECK (amount > 0),

    currency TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'INR',

    category TEXT NOT NULL,

    merchant TEXT,

    expense_date DATE NOT NULL,

    description TEXT,

    invoice_number TEXT,

    receipt_path TEXT,

    status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'submitted'
        CHECK (
            status IN (
                'draft',
                'submitted',
                'in_review',
                'approved',
                'rejected',
                'reimbursed'
            )
        ),

    policy_status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'pending'
        CHECK (
            policy_status IN (
                'pending',
                'compliant',
                'violation',
                'not_applicable'
            )
        ),

    risk_level TEXT
        CHECK (
            risk_level IS NULL
            OR risk_level IN ('low', 'medium', 'high')
        ),

    ai_recommendation TEXT,

    ai_summary TEXT,

    ai_analysis JSONB,

    submitted_at TIMESTAMPTZ,

    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),

    updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW()
);
```

The `ai_analysis` JSONB field can hold structured LLM results such as:

```json
{
  "category": "Accommodation",
  "confidence": 0.96,
  "policy_compliant": false,
  "duplicate_detected": false,
  "anomaly": true,
  "budget_impact": "high",
  "recommendation": "finance_review",
  "reasons": [
    "Hotel expense exceeds policy limit",
    "Department budget utilization is high"
  ]
}
```

No separate AI database tables are necessary for the MVP.

---

# 19. Table 7 — expense_approvals

Purpose:

Stores actual human approval actions.

SQL:

```sql
CREATE TABLE public.expense_approvals (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),

    expense_id UUID NOT NULL
        REFERENCES public.expenses(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,

    approver_id UUID NOT NULL
        REFERENCES public.profiles(id) ON DELETE RESTRICT,

    approval_order INTEGER NOT NULL
        CHECK (approval_order > 0),

    status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'pending'
        CHECK (
            status IN (
                'pending',
                'approved',
                'rejected',
                'skipped'
            )
        ),

    comment TEXT,

    acted_at TIMESTAMPTZ,

    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),

    UNIQUE (expense_id, approval_order)
);
```

Example:

```text
Expense #1024

Manager:
APPROVED

Finance:
PENDING
```

---

# 20. Table 8 — audit_logs

Purpose:

Stores important system events.

SQL:

```sql
CREATE TABLE public.audit_logs (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),

    user_id UUID
        REFERENCES public.profiles(id) ON DELETE SET NULL,

    expense_id UUID
        REFERENCES public.expenses(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,

    action TEXT NOT NULL,

    old_value JSONB,

    new_value JSONB,

    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW()
);
```

Example actions:

```text
expense_submitted
expense_updated
policy_checked
expense_approved
expense_rejected
expense_escalated
budget_updated
ai_analysis_completed
```

---

# 21. Database Creation Order

Create tables in this exact order:

```text
1. departments
2. profiles
3. budgets
4. expense_policies
5. approval_rules
6. expenses
7. expense_approvals
8. audit_logs
```

Reason:

There are foreign-key dependencies between these tables.

---

# 22. Indexes

After creating the tables:

```sql
CREATE INDEX idx_profiles_department
ON public.profiles(department_id);

CREATE INDEX idx_expenses_employee
ON public.expenses(employee_id);

CREATE INDEX idx_expenses_department
ON public.expenses(department_id);

CREATE INDEX idx_expenses_status
ON public.expenses(status);

CREATE INDEX idx_expenses_date
ON public.expenses(expense_date);

CREATE INDEX idx_expenses_category
ON public.expenses(category);

CREATE INDEX idx_expense_approvals_expense
ON public.expense_approvals(expense_id);

CREATE INDEX idx_expense_approvals_approver
ON public.expense_approvals(approver_id);

CREATE INDEX idx_audit_logs_expense
ON public.audit_logs(expense_id);
```

---

# 23. RLS

Enable RLS on all application tables:

```sql
ALTER TABLE public.profiles ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE public.departments ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE public.budgets ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE public.expense_policies ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE public.approval_rules ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE public.expenses ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE public.expense_approvals ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE public.audit_logs ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
```

Proper role-based policies should later be added for:

```text
employee
manager
finance
admin
```

---

# 24. Supabase Storage

Receipt files should use Supabase Storage.

Bucket:

```text
expense-receipts
```

Bucket should be:

```text
Private
```

It can be created with:

```sql
INSERT INTO storage.buckets (id, name, public)
VALUES ('expense-receipts', 'expense-receipts', false);
```

Verify:

```sql
SELECT id, name, public
FROM storage.buckets
WHERE id = 'expense-receipts';
```

Storage path example:

```text
expense-receipts/
    <employee_id>/
        <expense_id>/
            receipt.pdf
```

The PostgreSQL table stores only:

```text
expenses.receipt_path
```

Do not store the actual PDF/image inside PostgreSQL.

---

# 25. Important Security Rule

The Supabase `service_role` key must NEVER be exposed to the React/TSX frontend.

Correct:

```text
React
   ↓
FastAPI
   ↓
Supabase
```

The FastAPI backend can hold privileged Supabase credentials.

Incorrect:

```text
React
   ↓
service_role key
```

