# 33. Final Product Workflow

```text
ADMIN
 │
 ├── Create departments
 ├── Define budgets
 ├── Define policies
 └── Define approval rules
 │
 ▼
EMPLOYEE
 │
 ├── Upload receipt
 ├── Manual entry
 └── Verify AI-extracted data
 │
 ▼
AI / BACKEND
 │
 ├── Extract expense information
 ├── Categorize expense
 ├── Check policy
 ├── Detect duplicate
 ├── Analyze anomaly
 ├── Calculate budget impact
 ├── Generate forecast
 └── Generate recommendation
 │
 ▼
MANAGER / FINANCE / ADMIN
 │
 ├── Review AI analysis
 ├── View receipt
 ├── View budget impact
 └── Approve / Reject / Escalate
 │
 ▼
SUPABASE
 │
 ├── Update expense
 ├── Update approval
 └── Create audit log
 │
 ▼
DASHBOARD
 │
 ├── Budget utilization
 ├── Pending approvals
 ├── Forecast
 ├── Risks
 └── AI insights
```

# 34. Core Principle for Development

Keep the architecture simple:

```text
LLM = Understanding + Explanation + Recommendation

FastAPI/Python = Business logic + calculations + orchestration

Supabase = Data + authentication + receipt storage

React/TSX = User interface
```

Most importantly:

> **Do not use the LLM for calculations that normal code can perform accurately.**

For example:

```text
Budget remaining
= Budget - Approved Expenses
```

should be calculated by Python/SQL.

The LLM can then explain:

> "The department has ₹7.6 lakh remaining and is projected to exceed its annual allocation based on current spending trends."

